

1- ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENT--- to create/ train an application which can perform its own task without any human intervention 
  e.g--- netfix recommendation system,a self driving car,amazon shopping recommendation etc


2- MACHINE LEARNING----- A subset of AI that provides stats tools to analyze,visualize,predict or forcast a specific data
    
3- DEEP LEARNING-----a subset of Machine learning to mimick the human brain using multi layerd neuro network
4- DATA SCIENCE --- a field of using data, statistics, programming and analytical techniques to find useful information for  better decisions.


                TYPES OF MACHINE LEARNING TECHNIQUES

1-Supervised ML---In supervised learning, you give the computer data + the correct answers (labels) 
2-Unsupervised ML --- you give the computer data but no correct answers, so the computer has to find patterns,groups or relationships by itself

3-Reinforcement ML --- The computer (called an agent) interacts with an environment and learns by receiving rewards or penalties.

